    "type_designations": ["420 Series", "TS420 Series", "Sentinel 420", "Cerberus 420", "Theia 420"],
    "module_designation": "Not applicable",
    "description": "Family of mains-powered, single-interval, automatic weighing instruments (checkweighers, Category X) designated the TS420 Series, designed to weigh packs dynamically. The instruments comprise a cabinet, touch screen user interface (HMI), in-feed and out-feed conveyors, a weighing unit with weigh conveyor, mechanical handling facilities and sorting devices, and may be equipped with a metal detector. Constructed in stainless steel on a fabricated floor-standing frame with adjustable feet; photocells on the frame detect packs; the control cabinet houses the electrical hardware including the A/D board and flash card memory holding legally relevant parameters. Models are designated 420 Series with functional prefixes (e.g. Sentinel 420 for stand alone, Cerberus 420 for metal detection, Theia 420 for X-ray). Weighing device is a strain gauge load cell below the centre of the weigh conveyor. Devices: semi-automatic zero setting, zero tracking, initial zero setting, pre-set tare, data storage device. Interfaces: Ethernet and USB. CF card, HMI board and load cell connection to the electronics are sealed via a tamper-evident solution. Alternatively, any compatible load cell may be used provided it has a respective OIML R60 Certificate of Conformity with the necessary data for the declaration of compatibility of modules, is not a load cell with digital output, has n_lc, Y, Z the same or better than the tested HBM PW16AC3 (Emax = 30 kg), has the same design and material, uses no oil damper, and has sensitivity greater than 0.33 uV/div. Legally relevant software consists of two parts (HMI and Controller) held in read-only directories; parameters are secured by password and a non-editable Parameter Modification Counter, and calibration by password and a Calibration Count, both held on the Controller."
  },
